        {
          "sid": "body-t1-s01",
          "c": "我頭好痛。",
          "j": "ngo5 tau4 hou2 tung3.",
          "e": "My head really hurts.",
          "note": "To say a body part hurts, name it as the topic then describe it — 我頭好痛 (ngo5 tau4 hou2 tung3) \"my head really hurts\", literally \"I, head, very hurts\". No \"my\" (嘅 ge3) needed. 痛 (tung3) is \"to hurt / be sore\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "my"
            },
            {
              "c": "頭",
              "j": "tau4",
              "e": "head"
            },
            {
              "c": "好痛",
              "j": "hou2 tung3",
              "e": "really hurts"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "body-t1-s02",
          "c": "我眼好攰。",
          "j": "ngo5 ngaan5 hou2 gui6.",
          "e": "My eyes are very tired.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "my"
            },
            {
              "c": "眼",
              "j": "ngaan5",
              "e": "eyes"
            },
            {
              "c": "好攰",
              "j": "hou2 gui6",
              "e": "very tired"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "body-t1-s03",
          "c": "洗手要用水。",
          "j": "sai2 sau2 jiu3 jung6 seoi2.",
          "e": "Washing hands requires water.",
          "note": "用 (jung6) is \"to use\" — 用水 (jung6 seoi2) \"use water\". And 要 (jiu3) here means \"needs / requires\" rather than personal \"want\" — 洗手要用水 (sai2 sau2 jiu3 jung6 seoi2) \"washing hands needs water\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "洗手",
              "j": "sai2 sau2",
              "e": "wash hands"
            },
            {
              "c": "要",
              "j": "jiu3",
              "e": "need / require"
            },
            {
              "c": "用",
              "j": "jung6",
              "e": "use"
            },
            {
              "c": "水",
              "j": "seoi2",
              "e": "water"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "body-t1-s04",
          "c": "我心好痛。",
          "j": "ngo5 sam1 hou2 tung3.",
          "e": "My heart hurts (sad).",
          "note": "心痛 (sam1 tung3), literally \"heart hurts\", usually means *emotional* pain — heartache or distress — rather than a physical heart problem, like English \"it breaks my heart\". (Ties to the 心 sam1 \"heart\" feeling-words.)",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "my"
            },
            {
              "c": "心",
              "j": "sam1",
              "e": "heart"
            },
            {
              "c": "好痛",
              "j": "hou2 tung3",
              "e": "really hurts"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "body-t1-s05",
          "c": "佢腳受傷。",
          "j": "keoi5 goek3 sau6 soeng1.",
          "e": "His leg is injured.",
          "note": "受傷 (sau6 soeng1) means \"to get injured / be hurt\" — 佢腳受傷 (keoi5 goek3 sau6 soeng1) \"his leg is injured\". Note 腳 (goek3) covers both \"leg\" and \"foot\" in Cantonese.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "佢",
              "j": "keoi5",
              "e": "he / she"
